  "goodToKnow": "Der Passant (die Passantin) is a passer-by, common in news reports: Passanten leisteten Erste Hilfe (passers-by gave first aid). Street interviews are often called Passantenbefragungen. It's a weak noun: den Passanten. In Germany, failing to help in an emergency (unterlassene Hilfeleistung) is a criminal offence, so passers-by are legally required to help where reasonable. From French passant. Plural: die Passanten."
